## Overview

The connection status indicator's glow animation was barely visible in light mode due to hard-coded green colors that lacked sufficient contrast against the purple/blue gradient header background. This PR improves the animation to be clearly visible in both light and dark themes.

## Problem

The original implementation used a single `@keyframes glow` animation with hard-coded RGBA colors:

```css
@keyframes glow {
  0% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.6); }
  70% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 8px rgba(16, 185, 129, 0); }
  100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(16, 185, 129, 0); }
}
```

This green glow appeared washed out in light mode's vibrant gradient header, making the connection status difficult to notice.

## Solution

### 1. Theme-Aware Glow Colors

Added CSS custom properties for glow colors that adapt to the current theme:

**Light Mode:**
```css
--glow-color-connected: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
--glow-color-error: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
--glow-color-warning: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
```

**Dark Mode:**
```css
--glow-color-connected: rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.6);
--glow-color-error: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.6);
--glow-color-warning: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.6);
```

### 2. Enhanced Animations

Created separate animations for each connection state with dual-layer box-shadows for better depth:

```css
@keyframes glow-connected {
  0% { 
    box-shadow: 0 0 4px 2px var(--glow-color-connected),
                0 0 0 0 var(--glow-color-connected);
  }
  50% { 
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px 4px var(--glow-color-connected),
                0 0 0 6px transparent;
  }
  100% { 
    box-shadow: 0 0 4px 2px var(--glow-color-connected),
                0 0 0 0 var(--glow-color-connected);
  }
}
```

### 3. Consistent Timing

Standardized animation timing to 1.6s ease-in-out across all connection states (connected, disconnected, connecting) for visual coherence.

